--- !u!114 &1236930358
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1236930355}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f553d6ffa03804636a6e8eb25ce66cb9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SphereDialogue
  lines:
  - Fruit sorbet tastes really different from any other ice cream texture-wise.
  - Because there's no milk or cream added, just frozen fruit syrup.
  - I highly recommend having this in a really hot summer day. Fruit sorbets are
    extremely refreshing and hydrating due to their ingredients.
  - This ice cream has a really long history as well.
  - "Fruit sorbet began as chilled fruit syrups and snow-cooled drinks in ancient
    Persia around 550\u2013530 BC before evolving into a formal frozen dessert."
  - "Persians used to store winter snow and ice in ice houses (yakhch\u0101ls) to
    pair with fruit syrups and sweet drinks."
  - 'Snow and ice were also used in China, Greece, and the Middle East to chill beverages
    and fruit juices. '
  - In late 17 century, which is hundreds of years later, printed recipes for flavored
    ices and sorbetti appeared in European works.
  - Yum.
--- !u!1 &1289804575 stripped
GameObject:
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 8416272007918961125, guid: 393528a58ce274e66b2043aff7e98c7b, type: 3}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 1399527803}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
--- !u!114 &1289804579
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1289804575}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f553d6ffa03804636a6e8eb25ce66cb9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SphereDialogue
  lines:
  - Scoop ice cream!
  - They're so round and smooth and cute...
  - They're created in the perfect shape for licking! *slurp*
  - But did you know that before the scoop spoons are invented,
  - 'People used regular spoons to serve ice cream balls, which is slow, inconvenient,
    not perfect sphere, '
  - and might cause the scoops to stick together?
  - In 1876, George William Clewell worked with Valentine Clad and created a spoon
    dedicated for scoop ice cream.
  - The spoon requires two hands to work, one to hold the handle and another to turn
    a key or mechanism to release the ice cream.
  - Later in 1897,  a black inventor called Cralle saw servers struggle with ice
    cream sticking to utensils while working as a porter in Pittsburgh.
  - He then invented a better spoon featured a built-in scraper mechanism for easy,
    one-handed operation and kept ice cream from sticking.
  - Isn't it so fascinating to know the history behind this cute ice cream ball?
  - That's it for this ice cream, enjoy your next parkour.
--- !u!64 &1289804580
