--- !u!114 &1291361639
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1291361635}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f553d6ffa03804636a6e8eb25ce66cb9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SphereDialogue
  lines:
  - EGG WAFFLE ICECREAM!!!
  - I know there're a lot of Chinese in this class. You SHOULD have had this in some
    point in your life.
  - They're kinda expensive, and you usually only have it when you're having fun
    with your friends in a mall or something.
  - If you're an American you'd think it's really cheap, since 20rmb is less than
    4 bucks.
  - Anyways, egg waffle ice cream is a combination of two separate desserts.
  - Egg waffle (jidanzai in mandarin or gai daan jai in cantonese) emerged on the
    streets of Hong Kong in the 1950s.
  - Any Cantonese here?
  - ' A popular origin story says shopkeepers or hawkers mixed cracked, unsold, or
    leftover eggs with flour, sugar, and evaporated milk to prevent waste.'
  - In the 2010s, shops and chefs began rolling warm egg waffles into cones or wrapping
    them around scoops of ice cream and gelato.
  - The hot crispy egg puffs and the soft cool ice cream bursting in your mouth is
    a lifetime experience.
  - You gotta try it.
