--- !u!114 &1766349265
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1766349260}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f553d6ffa03804636a6e8eb25ce66cb9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SphereDialogue
  lines:
  - Fruit sorbet tastes really different from any other ice cream texture-wise.
  - Because there's no milk or cream added, just frozen fruit syrup.
  - I highly recommend having this in a really hot summer day. Fruit sorbets are
    extremely refreshing and hydrating due to their ingredients.
  - This ice cream has a really long history as well.
  - "Fruit sorbet began as chilled fruit syrups and snow-cooled drinks in ancient
    Persia around 550\u2013530 BC before evolving into a formal frozen dessert."
  - "Persians used to store winter snow and ice in ice houses (yakhch\u0101ls) to
    pair with fruit syrups and sweet drinks."
  - 'Snow and ice were also used in China, Greece, and the Middle East to chill beverages
    and fruit juices. '
  - In late 17 century, which is hundreds of years later, printed recipes for flavored
    ices and sorbetti appeared in European works.
  - Yum.
